# Ports the system disk carries installed: make system-disk builds their
# packages and install-to-image puts them on the disk, recorded in
# /var/db/pkg, so pkg lists, verifies and removes them like any other
# package. One port a line: name, name@flavor or category/name. A port
# that needs a download (DISTDIR, ~/Downloads/sources) makes the disk
# build need it too; one this machine cannot build (no C toolchain yet)
# is skipped. "PORT with OTHER": PORT only when OTHER is on the disk.

hello
# GNU as and ld (and ar, nm, objdump ...) running on the system: native
# Free Pascal on AArch64 assembles and links with them. Skipped without
# the C toolchain (make c-toolchain).
binutils
# OpenGL and OpenGL ES (Mesa, software rendering) with their tests and
# demonstrations. Skipped without the C toolchain.
gldemos
# The Lua interpreter and SQLite's shell: ported C programs to run in the
# terminal. Skipped without the C toolchain.
lua
sqlite3
# Doom (doomgeneric) and Freedoom's game data for it. Doom is skipped
# without the C toolchain, and Freedoom (nothing to build) goes with it.
doomgeneric
freedoom with doomgeneric
